lutions pod has  a step by step button so we can click  that and see what this looks like so  first of all it pops up it's nice and  colorful and we've got first thing you  see we have it's step by step but we  give step one here what you can do is  you can click through step by step and  you will get hints about what the next  step will be and then factor the  left-hand side okay you can click the  next step and you can see what the the  result of that hint would be so if we  factored the left-hand side of this  previous equation this is what we would  get then we can continue stepping  through you know separate the equations  solve the one equation 4x  look at the second equation solve it for  X and then that would be our solution  which matches the solutions found here  if I go back to this step button you'll  see in this top right-hand corner we  have alternate methods so not only do we  show one particular method but we try  and show all of the methods that make  sense for each particular problem so  here we have completing the square or  using the quadratic formula we also try  and sort these methods in a way that  makes sense so the easiest or shortest  steps would be first and then the more  complicated or you know formulaic would  be shown later if you want to skip going  through step by step we also have this  show all steps button and that gives all  the steps all at once so you can scroll  all the way down to find the answer  so steps for things like solutions and  things like derivatives and integrals  steps for those things make sense  because there are there are certain  algorithms that we we use as people that  we learn in school there's certain  algorithms that we use to solve a  particular type of problem so solving  factoring or solving you know how to  compute the average of a list of numbers  but there's some things that are a  little more esoteric like proofs where  there's not necessarily a a particular  algorithm that we always follow but we 